(vector (map (:db/id -1)
  (:adr/id "adr-2608101200-murakumo-model-hosting-runtime-storage-reporting")
  (:adr/doc-type "adr")
  (:adr/source-format "edn")
  (:adr/title "murakumo.cloud model hosting Phase 5 — ONNX/safetensors runtime, encrypted dual-region bytes, and jurisdiction reporting outbox")
  (:adr/topic "murakumo-model-hosting-runtime-storage-reporting")
  (:adr/status "accepted")
  (:adr/date "2026-08-10")
  (:adr/last-verified "2026-08-10")
  (:adr/authoritative true)
  (:adr/deciders (vector "Jun Kawasaki"))

  (:adr/authoritative-for
  (vector "ONNX and safetensors-transformers promotion into the Murakumo fleet"
   "private model-byte encryption and APAC/WNAM application-level replication"
   "US, UK, and Japan external-report preparation, approval, delivery, and receipt boundaries"))

  (:adr/decision-summary
  (vector "D1: ONNX and safetensors-transformers use a fixed offline image; repository code, arbitrary argv, and custom auto_map are forbidden"
   "D2: every model block and revision root is written with a customer-supplied SSE-C key to both APAC primary and WNAM replica before publication succeeds"
   "D3: reads fail over to the replica and scheduled reconciliation repairs one-sided retry windows without making D1 the bytes authority"
   "D4: external reports require a typed trust case, fixed jurisdiction/destination pair, human draft, distinct human approval, and recorded receipt"
   "D5: NCMEC and NCA connectors remain fail-closed until authority credentials and legal onboarding exist; Japan IHC uses a manual-portal receipt path"
   "D6: the production boundary is cloud-murakumo merge d1f7957216ea8e5b6e3c20fa81360e619e613da0, D1 migration 0006, Worker version 7ab2b884-743e-40c9-b398-9ff6ec92f704, and the gad runtime image sha256:fc6753b11035a6e79fffd3692acb834c18b72ca3e064b52e64e16e09d14aec66"))

  (:adr/verify
  (vector "curl https://murakumo.cloud/api/v1/model-hosting | jq .phase_5"
   "wrangler d1 migrations list murakumo-model-registry --remote"
   "wrangler r2 bucket info murakumo-model-blocks"
   "wrangler r2 bucket info murakumo-model-blocks-replica"
   "launchctl print gui/$(id -u)/cloud.murakumo.model-fleet"
   "ssh gad 'docker image inspect murakumo-model-runtime:phase5'"))

  (:adr/body
  "# Context

Phase 4 proved isolated dynamic loading and GGUF rollout, but explicitly left ONNX
and safetensors deployment unsupported. Private/gated bytes were access-controlled
but not protected with an operator-held encryption key, storage had one region, and
trust cases had no governed handoff to external reporting channels.

# Decision

ONNX promotion accepts exactly one top-level graph. The fixed CPU ONNX Runtime image
derives named inputs from the graph and executes bounded probes. Safetensors promotion
requires a standard Transformers config/tokenizer/weight bundle, forbids Python files
and `config.auto_map`, and loads only local files with `trust_remote_code=false` and
`use_safetensors=true`. Both formats run as an unprivileged user with a read-only root,
bounded tmpfs/resources, dropped Linux capabilities, no-new-privileges, loopback-only
canary and production ports, checksum revalidation, health gate and retained rollback.

R2 remains the immutable bytes authority. The Worker requires a 256-bit SSE-C key and
two distinct bucket bindings. A put succeeds only after encrypted writes to APAC primary
and WNAM replica; reads prefer primary and fail over to replica, and deletes cover both.
Scheduled reconciliation records and repairs one-sided failures. This is application-
level replication, not a claim that one Cloudflare R2 bucket natively replicates regions.

External reporting is an outbox, not automatic legal adjudication. A moderator drafts
from an existing trust case and a different moderator approves. Code fixes the allowed
pairs to US/NCMEC CyberTipline and UK/NCA CSEA for credentialed CSAM reporting, and
JP/Internet Hotline Center for manual portal handoff. Runner endpoints cannot be supplied
by repository metadata or arbitrary request data. Every claim, retry, failure, external
reference and CID receipt is recorded. Legal counsel/authority onboarding still decides
whether a concrete case is reportable and supplies connector credentials.

# Evidence

`network-awai/cloud-murakumo#51` merged as `d1f7957`. Remote D1 migration 0006 is
applied and the Phase 5 capability is live in Worker version
`7ab2b884-743e-40c9-b398-9ff6ec92f704`. The empty pre-existing object plane required no
plaintext backfill. R2 reports primary APAC and replica WNAM with zero objects in each.
The SSE-C key is a Worker secret with a Keychain escrow; the token-signing secondary is
escrowed in Kagi. The gad image was rebuilt from the merge and returned deterministic
ONNX output `[[[1.0,1.0]]]` and safetensors text `hello 200` under the production sandbox
flags. Scanner and fleet LaunchAgents run from the merged component checkout.

Targeted Phase 5, fleet, external-report and model-hosting tests pass. The repository-wide
test command still has unrelated pre-existing failures for a MusicGen pricing declaration
and a generated model-hosting asset, so it is not recorded as a full-suite pass.

# Remaining boundary

No user model is deployed until a clean revision receives governed promotion. NCMEC/NCA
automatic delivery is implemented but deliberately inactive without authority-issued
credentials and completed legal onboarding. Japan remains a human portal handoff with a
required receipt. This ADR does not determine ownership, illegality, or a statutory duty
for an individual case.

# Manifest

root's `cloud-murakumo` pin advances separately through the guarded single-entry server
workflow to `d1f7957216ea8e5b6e3c20fa81360e619e613da0`.")))
